#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:5
msgid "Samsung S2M Series PMIC RGB LED Driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:8
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:10
msgid ""
"The RGB LED on the S2M series PMIC hardware features a three-channel LED "
"that is grouped together as a single device. Furthermore, it supports 8-bit "
"brightness control for each channel. This LED is typically used as a status "
"indicator in mobile devices. It also supports various parameters for "
"hardware patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:16
msgid ""
"The hardware pattern can be programmed using the \"pattern\" trigger, using "
"the hw_pattern attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:20
msgid "/sys/class/leds/<led>/repeat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:22
msgid ""
"The hardware supports only indefinitely repeating patterns. The repeat "
"attribute must be set to -1 for hardware patterns to function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:26
msgid "/sys/class/leds/<led>/hw_pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:28
msgid "Specify a hardware pattern for the RGB LEDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:30
msgid ""
"The pattern is a series of brightness levels and durations in milliseconds. "
"There should be only one non-zero brightness level. Unlike the results "
"described in leds-trigger-pattern, the transitions between on and off states "
"are smoothed out by the hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:35
msgid "Simple pattern::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../leds/leds-s2m-rgb.rst:47
msgid ""
"As described in leds-trigger-pattern, it is also possible to use zero-length "
"entries to disable the ramping mechanism."
msgstr ""

